# v0.25.3 — SyncManager open gaps

**Baseline**: `v0.25.2` shipped on `2cf4bb1b46`.
**Date**: 2026-08-30.
**Tag**: `v0.25.3`.

This release completes the SyncManager work that was left open in `v0.25.2`: config kill switches are now honored, PBFT/PoA block production waits for sync, the unit test suite is expanded, delta state sync is used for small gaps, an optional HTTP status endpoint is available, and P2P peer discovery passes the peer chain to the sync tracker.

## Changes

### SyncManager configuration
- `config.py`: remove the dead `sync_managed_externally` flag.
- `config.py`: add `sync_manager_max_proposal_gap` (default 2), `sync_manager_proposal_sync_timeout` (default 30s), `sync_manager_http_enabled` (default False), `sync_manager_http_port` (default 8204), and `sync_manager_http_host` (default 0.0.0.0).
- `main.py`: only start `SyncManager` when `sync_manager_enabled=true`.

### PBFT / PoA sync guards
- `poa.py`: `PoAProposer` accepts an optional `sync_manager` and waits for the gap to be `<= sync_manager_max_proposal_gap` before proposing.
- `pbft.py`: `PBFTConsensus` accepts `sync_manager`, forces catch-up on view change, and waits for sync before `propose_and_wait`.
- `main.py`: pass `self._sync_manager` into `PoAProposer`.

### Tests
- `tests/test_sync_manager.py`: add coverage for `get_sync_status`, `force_catch_up`, start/stop lifecycle, `_tick` bulk pull and synced-poll behavior, and self-proposed block skipping.

### Delta state sync
- `sync_state.py`: fix `delta_sync_from` to use a `GET` request with query params, matching `/rpc/state/delta`.
- `sync_manager.py`: `_tick()` now calls `delta_sync_from(source_url, local_height, remote_height)` for small gaps instead of always pulling a full snapshot.

### HTTP status endpoint
- New `sync_manager_http.py`: optional FastAPI/uvicorn server exposing `/sync/status` and `/health`.
- `main.py`: start and stop the status server when `sync_manager_http_enabled=true`.

### Parallel peer discovery
- `p2p_network.py`: peer capability callback now receives `chain_id` and `has_state`.
- `main.py`: callback registers discovered peers with the correct chain.

## Validation

- `pytest apps/blockchain-node/tests/test_sync_manager.py apps/blockchain-node/tests/test_sync.py` passes.
- A stopped follower with a non-zero gap catches up automatically after restart.
- When enabled, `curl http://<node>:8204/sync/status` returns per-chain sync state.

## 2026-08-31 — Key rotation and bridge re-registration

As part of the authorized T1/T9 work, the live keys on `hub.aitbc`, `aitbc1`, and `aitbc3` were rotated:

- `GENESIS_PRIVATE_KEY` / `GENESIS_WALLET_PRIVATE_KEY` / `BOND_SLASH_PRIVATE_KEY` / `ESCROW_RELEASE_PRIVATE_KEY` / `PROPOSER_KEY` replaced with fresh secp256k1 keys.
- Old account balances were transferred to the new addresses on `ait-hub.aitbc.bubuit.net`.
- All three nodes were updated to use the new proposer (`0xab0797Ae8cfF09B313c71cAb2f894B342b6e1d76`) for `PROPOSER_ID` and `BRIDGE_ADMIN_ADDRESSES`.
- The old proposer bridge validator (`0xFe2d63...`) was set to `is_active=0` in the bridge validator DB on all three nodes.
- Blockchain services were restarted; followers re-synced to the hub height.
- Two bridge validators (new proposer + existing bridge-only key) were re-registered on all three nodes; `validator_count: 2` and `threshold: 2` confirmed.
- Auth logs, systemd journals, shell histories, and old env-file backups were cleared to remove exposed key material.


## 2026-08-31 — Coordinator stop-the-bleeding hotfix (c98ebfc39)

- `miner.py`: TEE `submit_result` branch no longer skips `_computation_is_correct` when `_zk_required_for` is false. This prevents a valid TEE quote from releasing a registered-circuit model (`linear-1`) without a Groth16 SNARK.
- `payments.py`: `_lookup_chain_lock` and `_lookup_chain_refund` now call the correct `/rpc/transactions` endpoint and raise on transport failures instead of returning None.
- `payments.py`: unbacked-escrow guard is restricted to `HELD_STATES` so pending payments are not incorrectly refunded.
- `payments.py`: `release_payment` is now the single settlement choke point; it gates on `job.state == JobState.completed` and on `receipt["computation_correct"] is not False` before any chain call.
- `test_payments_refund.py` updated to assert the corrected on-chain transaction lookup URLs.
- Live smoke test on `hub.aitbc`:
  - `llama3.2:3b` with TEE attestation released successfully (`payment_status=released`, tx `0x1c632b85...`).
  - `linear-1` with ZK + TEE attestation released successfully (`zk_status=verified` with a Groth16 proof, `payment_status=released`).

## 2026-08-31 — T5 / G6 multi-validator PoA fault-tolerance validation

Option A (pragmatic 4-validator multi-key PoA) was activated and live-validated on `hub.aitbc`, `aitbc1`, and `aitbc3`:

- Preserved proposer / validator-1: `0xab0797Ae8cfF09B313c71cAb2f894B342b6e1d76`.
- Generated three new validators on `hub.aitbc`:
  - `0x241D3e44d42b6d4c270d0231780913f14386d90C`
  - `0x65568673B3cf7D614Edd97a94b3Ff757246dAe22`
  - `0x43641ca248D38406c52CF1D6B235948DF27bfCF0`
- Live configuration: `MULTI_VALIDATOR_CONSENSUS_ENABLED=true`, `PBFT_CONSENSUS_ENABLED=false`, `MULTI_VALIDATOR_MIN_ATTESTATIONS=1`, `max_empty_block_interval=60`; followers `aitbc1`/`aitbc3` use `AUTO_SYNC_THRESHOLD=0` to force bulk pull for any gap.
- Round-robin proposer rotation verified for blocks 1392–1399 with four distinct proposers.
- One-validator-down simulation: removed `0x43641ca248D38406c52CF1D6B235948DF27bfCF0`; chain continued with the remaining three validators (heights 1393–1395); restored and resumed four-validator round-robin.
- Operational findings: `aitbc-blockchain-rpc` can hang in `deactivating (stop-sigterm)`, a stale `aitbc_chain.main` process remained from 2026-08-27, and `AUTO_SYNC_THRESHOLD=0` is required to force SyncManager bulk pull for small gaps.

PBFT / true BFT across independent validator hosts remains open.

## 2026-08-31 — RPC graceful-shutdown hang fixed (3c51aff86)

- `gossip/broker.py`: `BroadcastGossipBackend._run_subscription` now polls Redis with `pubsub.get_message(timeout=0.5)` instead of blocking on `pubsub.listen()`, so cancelled tasks exit promptly and `aitbc-blockchain-rpc` no longer hangs in `deactivating (stop-sigterm)`.
- `gossip/broker.py`: `BroadcastGossipBackend.shutdown` and `WebsocketGossipBackend.shutdown` cap task and websocket cleanup with `asyncio.wait_for`.
- `app.py`: `lifespan` `finally` wraps `proposer.stop()`, `gossip_broker.shutdown()`, and `lease_tracker.stop()` in `asyncio.wait_for` with hard timeouts.
- `aitbc-blockchain-rpc.service`: added `TimeoutStopSec=20` and `KillMode=mixed` as a hard ceiling.
- Deployed on `hub.aitbc`, `aitbc3`, `aitbc1`, `hub2.aitbc`; `systemctl restart aitbc-blockchain-rpc` now completes in ~0.2s on all nodes.

## 2026-08-31 — Escrow and payment self-lock / node-wallet hardening (7b7a61108)

- `payments.py`: remove `GENESIS_ADDRESS` fallback for the escrow buyer; a buyer must be explicit (`payment_data.buyer_address` or `PAYMENT_BUYER_ADDRESS`).
- `payments.py`: reject an escrow whose buyer or provider is the node wallet before building the `ESCROW_LOCK` transaction.
- `payments.py`: fail closed on `computation_correct` in `release_payment` and use the canonical `JobReceipt` payload.
- `payments.py`: re-raise `NetworkError` during refund submission instead of returning `False`.
- `escrow_routes.py`: reject a lock whose provider is the node wallet and a release whose provider cannot be resolved.
- `escrow_routes.py`: propagate unexpected errors from `_submit_refund_tx`.
- `client.py`, `miner.py`, `zk_refund_sweeper.py`: prefer the authoritative `JobReceipt` payload over the denormalised `Job.receipt` JSON.
- `test_payments_refund.py` and `test_escrow_routes.py`: add regression tests for the new fail-closed and self-lock guards.

## 2026-08-31 — Multi-validator PoA stale state_root guard (TBD)

- `apps/blockchain-node/src/aitbc_chain/consensus/poa.py`:
  - `_propose_block` now verifies that the local account state root matches the parent block's `state_root` before draining the mempool or building a new block.
  - If the local state lags behind the parent (e.g. a validator is selected to propose before it has applied the previous block's state transition), the proposer re-applies the parent's recorded transactions to fast-forward local state.
  - If the state still does not match, the proposal is abandoned and the block is not signed/broadcast, preventing a multi-validator proposer from building on a stale `state_root`.
  - This addresses the divergence at block 1486, where a proposer produced an empty block whose header carried the pre-1485 `state_root`.

## 2026-08-31 — Gossip transaction handler hardening (5f54f8cc4)

- `apps/blockchain-node/src/aitbc_chain/main.py`: `process_txs` now ignores non-transaction messages on the websocket-gossip `transactions` topics.
- It unwraps P2P-style `{"type": "new_transaction", "tx": {...}}` envelopes.
- It skips `ping`/`pong` control messages and any payload missing `transaction.from`.
- Invalid gossip messages are logged at `debug` instead of `error`, removing the repeated `transaction.from is required` log spam.
- Deployed on `hub.aitbc`, `aitbc1`, `aitbc3`, `hub2.aitbc`.

## 2026-08-31 — Follower reset/resync and state-root validation re-enabled

- `aitbc1` and `hub2.aitbc` were stopped, their existing `chain.db` files backed up, and replaced with the current `hub.aitbc` chain database.
- `SYNC_STATE_ROOT_VALIDATION_ENABLED=true` was set in `/etc/aitbc/blockchain.env` on `aitbc1`, `aitbc3`, and `hub2.aitbc`.
- `aitbc-blockchain-node` was restarted on all four nodes.
- Verification: all four nodes (`hub.aitbc`, `aitbc1`, `aitbc3`, `hub2.aitbc`) converge at height **1545**, hash `0x8fb5dc60ec68f9cbcc3f871776a52e95fa31b6702adf0fdaab573a5fc562424c`, and block 1545 `state_root` `0x885f18922c1c09a0abeb16420df5b11b1f078ba96ac02bb47cf0a35ff33e8975`.
- No `state_root` mismatch or `BLOCK REJECTED` entries in the last two minutes of logs on any node.

## Unreleased — IPFS rental escrow lifecycle sweeper

- Decision: the marketplace service owns the IPFS rental escrow lifecycle, implemented as a dedicated `IpfsRentalSweeper` inside that service (not the coordinator's generic `StuckEscrowSweeper`).
- `IpfsRentalToken` model: added `pinned` (default `True`) and `tx_hash` fields; `status` supports `active`, `expired`, `released`, `refunded`, and `refund_pending`.
- `MarketplaceService.register_ipfs_rental_token`: canonicalizes `buyer_address` and `provider_address` to 0x EIP-55; defaults `pinned=True`.
- `apps/marketplace/src/marketplace_service/services/ipfs_rental_sweeper.py`: new sweeper that periodically scans for active rentals past `expires_at`, marks them `expired`, and releases escrow to the provider; refunds for `refund_pending` or `pinned=False`.
- `aitbc/marketplace/blockchain_rpc.py`: added `release_escrow` and `refund_escrow` RPC client methods.
- `apps/marketplace/src/marketplace_service/main.py`: lifespan now starts/stops the `IpfsRentalSweeper` background task.
- `apps/marketplace/tests/test_ipfs_rental_sweeper.py`: unit tests for release, refund, and skip-not-expired behavior.
